{
	title: 'Notification history in the web menu',
	spec: 'The web menu exposes Notifications: a persistent, newest-first history of notifications, including local in-app notices and web pushes, available after transient notices disappear, reload, reconnect, and opening a notification. Each entry shows event time, session name, actual notice text, and its reason: completed, failed, question or approval requiring an answer, or an informational mid-turn update. Informational notify-tool updates must not be labelled needs your attention or imply that a final answer exists or an answer is required. Retain distinct events from the same session rather than replacing them with its latest notice. Store the notification record on the host before delivery so a backgrounded client can retrieve it on return; use stable event IDs to avoid reconnect duplicates. Entries link to the relevant conversation and, where a history record identifies the trigger, its block; visiting an entry does not erase the historical record. Question entries distinguish still awaiting an answer from already answered, and notification text remains readable even if the triggering session is closed or unavailable. Use bounded retention with its limit documented in the menu, preserve existing routing, permission, privacy, and draft guarantees, and show no secrets or tool outputs beyond the existing sanitized notification payload. History is authenticated private host state, never tracked repository content. The menu shows an accessible empty state and works on coarse-pointer phones with native keyboard and dialog behavior.',
	status: 'planned',
	notes: [
		'Current implementation distinguishes only done, failed, and attention. The mid-turn notify tool delivers attention although it neither ends the turn nor requests an answer, and common/notices labels attention as needs your attention. Local notices expire after five seconds, are replaced by session key, and are removed when clicked; the tabs menu has no notification history. Distinguish informational updates from questions at the event source rather than inferring meaning from model wording. OS notification history alone cannot recover local notices or guarantee access to dismissed pushes.'
	],
	needs: ['qm', 'm1', '5e']
}
